---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/site/DocumentLayout.astro';
import Disclosure from '../components/site/Disclosure.astro';
import Contact from '../components/site/Contact.astro';
export const prerender = true;
---

<DocumentLayout
  title="SalahSide Support"
  description="A little help getting your prayer times, focus, and membership settled."
>
  <div class="support-contact">
    <p><Contact /></p>
    <p>
      Include your app version, iOS version, selected city, and a short description of the issue.
      Please leave out sensitive information.
    </p>
  </div>
  <h2>Prayer times</h2>
  <Disclosure question="Why are my times different from my mosque's?"
    ><p>
      In SalahSide Settings, confirm your city, calculation method, Asr convention, high-latitude
      rule, and minute adjustments. The first release supports London, New York, Toronto, Dubai, and
      Kuala Lumpur and uses the selected city's time zone.
    </p><p>
      Compare with a timetable using the same conventions. High-latitude seasons, daylight saving,
      and local Ramadan conventions can change expected times. For Umm al-Qura Ramadan adjustments,
      check your local timetable and apply the appropriate Isha offset.
    </p></Disclosure
  >
  <Disclosure question="What does a prayer check-in mean?"
    ><p>
      Start prayer begins your own prayer flow. Mark completion yourself, or use Already prayed.
      Unlock for this prayer releases focus without recording a completed prayer. A past prayer
      without your action remains unmarked.
    </p></Disclosure
  >
  <h2>App focus and reminders</h2>
  <Disclosure question="How do I choose apps or turn focus off?"
    ><p>
      Open SalahSide Settings and allow optional Screen Time access, then choose targets in Apple's
      picker. Turn individual prayer focus switches on or off. Prayer times work with active
      membership even if Screen Time stays off.
    </p></Disclosure
  >
  <Disclosure question="How do I regain access to my apps?"
    ><p>
      Open SalahSide and choose Unlock for this prayer, or open Settings and Pause for one hour. You
      can also change the app selection or disable focus in Settings. If a shield cannot open
      SalahSide directly on your iOS version, open SalahSide from your Home Screen.
    </p><p>
      If restrictions persist, reopen SalahSide to refresh permissions and membership, then disable
      focus. Erase local data in SalahSide Settings clears its saved selections and app-owned
      restrictions. You can also revoke SalahSide's Screen Time permission in iOS Settings.
    </p></Disclosure
  >
  <Disclosure question="Why didn't I receive a reminder?"
    ><p>
      Enable reminders in SalahSide and allow notifications in iOS Settings → Notifications →
      SalahSide. Check iOS Focus and notification settings. Reopen the app to refresh the upcoming
      schedule. Permission, device settings, or device state can affect delivery.
    </p></Disclosure
  >
  <h2>Membership</h2>
  <Disclosure question="How do I restore a subscription?"
    ><p>
      Use Restore purchases in SalahSide with the Apple account that purchased the subscription.
      Membership requires a verified active subscription or trial. If Apple shows an active
      subscription but access remains unavailable, reopen the app and contact support with the error
      text; do not send payment-card information.
    </p></Disclosure
  >
  <Disclosure question="Why don't I see a three-day trial?"
    ><p>
      Apple decides eligibility for the selected subscription offer. An eligible exact three-day
      free trial is shown only after Apple confirms it. Otherwise you can purchase at the localized
      price shown in the app.
    </p></Disclosure
  >
  <Disclosure question="How do I cancel or request a refund?"
    ><p>
      Open iPhone Settings → your name → Subscriptions → SalahSide to manage renewal. Deleting the
      app does not cancel membership. See <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/118428"
        >Apple's cancellation instructions</a
      >. For a refund, follow <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/118223"
        >Apple's refund instructions</a
      >; Apple decides eligibility.
    </p></Disclosure
  >
  <h2>Widgets and local data</h2>
  <Disclosure question="Why does my affirmation widget ask me to open SalahSide?"
    ><p>
      The widget needs a saved, verified active membership. Open SalahSide to refresh access, then
      return to the widget. Check that the widget and app are installed together and use the same
      device.
    </p></Disclosure
  >
  <Disclosure question="How do I erase my data?"
    ><p>
      Open SalahSide Settings → Erase local data and confirm. This removes prayer settings,
      selections, and local check-in history and clears focus restrictions. It returns you to setup.
      Apple subscriptions and existing device backups are managed separately through Apple.
    </p></Disclosure
  >
  <p>
    For the full details, read our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/terms/"
      >Terms</a
    >.
  </p>
</DocumentLayout>
